You should probably try to apply the debian patches *before* you make your  
changes.
In case your changes alter the same part of the code as these patches,  
making them first almost guarantee that the patches won't apply properly  
(adding a single blank line in the context is enough to make patch fail).

Of course, you should aways try to compile an unpatched version first to  
be sure everything is alright (incl. Makefiles and such) and start from a  
copy of a compilable directory, but from what you said in your other post,  
I guess you already know how to compile and patch :-)

